<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Windsheim</h1><p class="st-meta">1248 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Bad Windsheim</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Franconian imperial city on the Aisch, surrounded by Hohenzollern lands, which adopted the Reformation and kept its freedom until 1802.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-windsheim">Windsheim</a> grew from a Frankish royal estate and later belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a> before returning to the Empire. It was recognised as an imperial city in the mid 13th century, around 1248, on the road between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> and Würzburg.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The town was governed by a council and lived from farming, wine, crafts and its market. It was surrounded by the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> margraves of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-brandenburg-ansbach">Ansbach</a>, on whom it depended for trade and with whom it often quarrelled. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-windsheim">Windsheim</a> adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in the 1520s and subscribed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg-confession">Augsburg Confession</a> soon after it was presented in 1530.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The city lost its freedom when it was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1802. Its saline springs later made it a spa, renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-windsheim">Bad Windsheim</a>, and it now hosts the Franconian Open-Air Museum of rural buildings.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-imperial-city-of-windsheim.jpg" alt="Free Imperial City of Windsheim" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Tilman2007 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bad_Windsheim-005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1248 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bad Windsheim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>East Franconian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Germany</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bad Windsheim</dd></dl></aside></div>
